ion/problem" "value" "If \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}b & a & -b \\\\ -b & a & b \\\\ -b & 0 & -b\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$x=[\\begin{aligned}-b \\\\ 0 \\\\ b\\end{aligned}],$\nfind $Ax.$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Ax=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977620/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b41ecc89373e476999967d44775f1e5d2483ca13c228fb372fccf0578374fca"} {"question" "q-318589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}b & a & -b \\\\ -b & a & b \\\\ -b & 0 & -b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-b \\\\ 0 \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (-b) & + & a\\cdot 0 & + & (-b)\\cdot b \\\\ (-b)\\cdot (-b) & + & a\\cdot 0 & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,b\\cdot b \\\\ (-b)\\cdot (-b) & + & 0\\cdot 0 & + & (-b)\\cdot b\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-{b}^{2} & + & 0 & + & (-{b}^{2}) \\\\ {b}^{2} & + & 0 & + & {b}^{2} \\\\ {b}^{2} & + & 0 & + & (-{b}^{2})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2{b}^{2} \\\\ 2{b}^{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977620/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b41ecc89373e476999967d44775f1e5d2483ca13c228fb372fccf0578374fca"} {"question" "q-318589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977620/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fb3aed41d993ccb88359d022459007480499c01394ef7647909ec349de6a891"} {"question" "q-318589" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widge